# GACAR citation policy

Cite Saudi regulations as GACAR, never as FAA material.

Correct:

- `GACAR § 91.3` — one space after §, part.section, at most one dot.
- `GACAR Part 91` — when referring to a whole part.

Never write:

- `14 CFR`, `FAR`, `FAA Part 91`, `FAA regulations` — these are FAA numbering. Rewrite as the corresponding GACAR citation and verify the mapping at gaca.gov.sa.
- `§91`, `§§ 91.3`, or `§ 91.3.1` — malformed section signs.
- `GACAR Part 999` or any part outside 1–199. The published GACAR index currently ends at Part 199 (Parts 175, 179, 183, and 193 exist). Verify a new part against the official GACAR index before citing it.

Also:

- Quote the paragraph you rely on; do not paraphrase a regulation and present it as a quotation.
- If you cannot verify a citation against the official GACAR publication, mark the claim as unverified instead of inventing a part number.
- `node scripts/gate.mjs` must report zero `gacar` findings before a content PR is ready.
